1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:05,000
There's a conversation we have to finish.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,500
What was it about?

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:09,740
It was about caring.

4
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:12,400
Oh?

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:15,100
Yes, caring.

6
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,580
I said that it makes me feel good

7
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:19,000
that you care about Michelle.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,800
Well, I do care about Michelle.

9
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,750
And it makes me feel good that you care about me.

10
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,800
You know I do.

11
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:32,600
You're a ... wonderful friend.

12
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:33,700
And it makes me feel good

13
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:38,270
that you care about us.

14
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:41,300
Well ... well,

15
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:41,700
I do, Harry.

16
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:45,400
It's only natural that if I care about Michelle

17
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:47,400
and I care about you,

18
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:50,300
then I care about us.

19
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,000
It's OK, Susan.

20
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,300
We had this part of the conversation

21
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:54,400
before Michelle and her friends arrived.

22
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:57,330
Now comes the good part.

23
00:00:57,330 --> 00:00:58,000
Like what?

24
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,300
Well, assume that if you care about Michelle

25
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:02,400
and you care about me

26
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:05,200
and you care about us,

27
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:07,700
that we can talk about us.

28
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:11,600
I mean--you and me.

29
00:01:11,600 --> 00:01:14,800
Isn't that right?

30
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:20,300
What are you trying to say, Harry?

31
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:24,600
What I'm trying to say ...

32
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:29,500
since this is so easy ....

33
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:53,900
Here are ten letters that express my feelings for you.

34
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:56,100
Don't be silly, Harry.

35
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:57,100
You want a hint?

36
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:58,600
It's two words.

37
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:02,300
You're making the game harder.

38
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:04,100
Can't you figure it out?

39
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:06,100
Seven letters ... two words ...

40
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:09,700
that express the feelings that I feel for you in my heart.

41
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:29,700
Harry, I get it! Harry

42
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:33,700
Well? Does that mean you'll marry me?

43
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:43,200
Is that a proposal, or are we just playing a game?

44
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:48,300
Sit down, Susan.

45
00:02:48,300 --> 00:03:05,300
There's something I have to ask you.

46
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:10,000
Susan, will you marry me?

47
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,400
It's such an important decision.

48
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:15,300
There's so many things to talk about.

49
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:18,930
There are three things that have to be done first, Harry.

50
00:03:18,930 --> 00:03:20,450
Three things?

51
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:24,400
First, we have to decide where to live.

52
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,100
Well, that's easy.

53
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:26,200
We talked about that earlier.

54
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:27,400
We'll live in New York.

55
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,190
All right.

56
00:03:29,190 --> 00:03:30,030
Second,

57
00:03:30,030 --> 00:03:34,300
we have to talk to Michelle together about being married.

58
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:36,130
We'll do that immediately.

59
00:03:36,130 --> 00:03:38,500
What's the third thing?

60
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:40,000
You have to ask for my father's permission.

61
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,900
Absolutely!

62
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:43,880
But first things first.

63
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:47,200
We have to go pick up Michelle.

64
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:52,000
Oh, I'm so happy, Harry!

65
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Not as happy as I am.
